In article <1992Feb17.151636.4353@midway.uchicago.edu> mehr@oskar.uchicago.edu (David Mehringer) writes:
>In article <trump.698333117@elaine27.Stanford.EDU> trump@elaine27.Stanford.EDU (Michael Jason Lewis) writes:
>>of it there's a (2x2?) square with space inside it.  And I occasionally get the
>>message that someone is counting money, but there don't seem to be any shops.
>
>It's a vault and contains a few hundred g.p.  The messages "You hear
>someone counting money" or "You hear the footsteps of a guard on
>patrol" indicate there is a vault on the level.  You can get in by
>searching for a secret door by a message on the floor "ad er um" or
>something like this with a few question marks interposed among the
>characters.  Open the secret door, you will usually have to search again
>and will find a "#" (small alcove) outside the secret door.  This alcove
>contains a teleport trap and if you step on this square it will teleport
>you to the vault (assuming you don't have magic resistance or teleport
>control).  Once you're in, it's usually a good idea to have a way out,
>unless you are willing to leave all of your gold there.

There is one important item to remember here.  These messages 'ad er? um' or
whatever, do NOT always lead to the teleport trap,  Search carefully, and you
may find a trapdoor, or a valuable level teleport trap...

